<title>PHILIPPINES: British Gas unit joins talks on gas project.</title>
<headline>British Gas unit joins talks on gas project.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine National Oil Co-Exploration Corp said on Friday it was discussing a possible joint venture with First Gas Holding Corp (FGHC) to lay a $70 million, 170 km onshore gas pipeline.</p>
<p>First Gas is a joint venture of First Philippine Holdings Corp and British Gas.</p>
<p>PNOC-EC president Rufino Bomasang told Reuters that the PNOC-EC applied to the energy department for authorisation to lay the country's first gas pipeline.</p>
<p>&quot;We are talking with FGHC for a joint venture,&quot; said PNOC-EC manager Rafael del Pilar.</p>
<p>The pipeline will carry natural gas from the Camago-Malampaya field in the southern Philippines, the country's first commercial gas find. - Manila newsroom 63 2 8418936 fax 8176267</p>
